1. `shared` — the invariant identity that every panel draws, in this order: type and overall proportions; how the decks sit relative to the outer envelope (the total deck count is not a count of exposed tiers); the profile from bow to stern with positions; the plan shape, including the stern width when a fact gives it; every innovation — what it is, its size and its position; every asymmetric part with its side. Bring in the identity sizes the facts give (widths, lengths, diameters, counts, pool or terrace sizes and heights). Prefer exact quantities to adjectives such as narrow, shallow or recessed.
