- `camera_family` is one of `beam`, `aerial`, `tracking`, `from_deck`, `macro`, `interior`.

### Gates

- **RULE — story:** dosage matches length (Step 1.11, one step of deviation per column with its reason in `story.notes`; type E has no obstacles); loops separated ≥ 20%; B16 is H5 and no other beat is; no `finished` room before A4; ≥ 2 valleys, peak at B16; every obstacle labelled [CONCEPT STORY]; character anchors 20–30 words; the last act ≥ 30% of the running time; type E nulls only as Step 1.0 allows.
- **RULE — script:** no voiceover fields and no keys outside the Output; cards ≤ 6 words, ≥ 1.5 s, one on screen at a time; a QUESTION card only as Step 1.2 allows; STAGE, SPEC, NAME and QUESTION cards ≤ 1 per 10 s on average; spec cards end with “· CONCEPT”; no forbidden words, no source identity, no real-world claims; beat targets sum to {video_length} ± 5%; disclaimer and end card present; beats are B0–B16 with a flash-forward and B1–B16 without one, in order; B0 present exactly when `hook_type` is E; story structure differs from the last 2 films; hook type differs from the last film; no repeated moment outside the declared list; PROGRESS ≤ 1 per state and ≤ 15% of the running time; every beat named in story (obstacles, loops, money shots) exists in `script.beats`; B0 is not a moment from B13–B16; two beats in the same state differ in at least 2 of location · time of day and light · camera family · action; each act has at least one location or time of day not seen in the previous act; at least 2 money shots outside the Step 1.9 list; every beat respects the `operational_limits` of the features it shows; every room in `beats[].rooms` exists in `yacht_bible.rooms`, and the rooms in the tour match the dosage; a flash-forward is dropped only as Step 1.11 allows.
- **WARN — editorial (reported, does not block):** a construction state (BS06–BS11) fills more than 2 consecutive beats; fewer than two interior money shots; an act share far from Step 1.10 in structure S1.
- **JUDGE — story (≥ 8/10):** every beat showable without words; obstacles plausible for shipbuilding (not for type E); central question answerable on screen (not for type E without a question).
- **JUDGE — wordless clarity (≥ 8/10):**

| Criterion | Points |
| --- | --- |
| Hook works in 3 s with sound off | 2 |
| Central question understood by ~10 s (image or card) | 2 |
| Each obstacle reads as sign → proof without words | 2 |
| Interior tour feels like a walkable path | 2 |
| Hero is the most beautiful moment and the first full reveal | 2 |

For type E the two criteria about the central question and the obstacles are replaced by: “Scale and transformation read without words” (2) and “The reveal ladder builds steadily to the hero” (2).

### Quality gate

- [ ] Central question visual and answerable (type E: may be absent)
- [ ] Obstacles show sign and proof (not for type E)
- [ ] Reveal ladder and room states respected
- [ ] Motifs and first–last rhyme planned
- [ ] Emotion curve ready for music selection
- [ ] No narration anywhere
- [ ] Story structure, hook type and concrete hook chosen; one opening, not two hooks
- [ ] Beat sheet covers idea → design → construction → completion → sea, exterior and interior (in the order of the chosen structure)
- [ ] Cards sparse and compliant
- [ ] Music brief and SFX plan complete
