`status`: `ok` when every beat and stop is covered and no conflict or unresolved use is open; `partial` when a conflict or an unresolved use is open (say what in `flags`); `fail` only when the input cannot be used (then `data` is `{}` and `flags` says why).

### Step B gates

- **RULE (code):** ids exist (rooms and zones in the design, locations in the selected Step A run); `script_id` matches the script; every `evidence` quote is found verbatim in its field; every use, light, detail and shot change points to a beat or stop the background serves; a room background matches the `set_state` the script gives, at a tour stop too; an exterior background serves uses of one build-state kind and one surface; an `unplated` or `unresolved` entry names the space and state the script gives its use; every room state the script names, every beat and every tour stop is covered; every `match_bare_beat` has its continuity entry; a conflict names a background or a beat; no two backgrounds alike (same space, state, build-state kind and surface, condition and composition); no real names; `status` is `partial` while a conflict or an unresolved use is open.
- **WARNING (code, a person decides):** a `bare` room whose text names a word of its finished materials; an exterior\'s `surroundings` that shares a word with the area\'s own design text; a tour room whose state the script does not give.
- **REVIEW (a person):** the mappings, the sharing, the role of each beat and every prompt are read and approved on the Locations screen before and while the images are rendered; no extra AI pass checks the meaning.
