`status`: `ok` when every beat and stop is covered and no conflict or unresolved use is open; `partial` when a conflict or an unresolved use is open, or something could not be covered (say what in `flags`); `fail` only when the input cannot be used (then `data` is `{}` and `flags` says why). `flags` holds anything else a person must read; it never replaces `conflicts`, `unresolved` or `assumptions`.

### Gates

- **RULE (code):** every `LOC` id once and used; ids exist (rooms and zones in the design, locations in this answer); `script_id` matches the script; every `evidence` quote is found verbatim in its field; every use, light, detail and shot change points to a beat or stop the background serves; a room background matches the `set_state` the script gives, at a tour stop too; an exterior background serves uses of one build-state kind and one surface; an `unplated` or `unresolved` entry names the space and state the script gives its use; every room state the script names, every beat and every tour stop is covered; every `match_bare_beat` has its continuity entry; a conflict names a background or a beat; no two backgrounds alike (same space, state, build-state kind and surface, condition and composition); no background id twice; a location detail never repeats a surface or fixture of its location; `fit` matches the beats that stand on each location (a beat at a build state holds the full yacht, a `scale_model` beat the scale model) and a place that holds the yacht, a module or a model is not smaller than it; an enclosed `kind` is `bounded` and never `open` overhead; no real names; `status` is `partial` while a conflict or an unresolved use is open; the prompt sent to render is the prompt shown and approved.
- **WARNING (code, a person decides):** two locations alike in every fixed field (kind, space, size, clear height, surfaces, equipment, palette), perhaps one place; a `bare` room whose text names a word of its finished materials; an exterior\'s `surroundings` that shares a word with the area\'s own design text; a tour room whose state the script does not give; a location text that names the yacht or a part of it; a composition that seems to describe a camera move; a background seen only briefly with many must-show details; an exterior background serving an `H1` beat; dimensions that are assumptions, unverified or short of the recommended working room.
- **REVIEW (a person):** the locations, the mappings, the sharing, the role of each beat and every prompt are read and approved on the Locations screen before and while the images are rendered; no extra AI pass checks the meaning.
