### Gates

- **RULE — story:** type E has no obstacles and its nulls only as Step 1.0 allows; loops separated ≥ 20%; B16 is H5 and no other beat is; no `finished` room before A4; emotion peaks at B16; every obstacle labelled [CONCEPT STORY]; every character anchor within its word limit.
- **RULE — script:** all 17 beats B0–B16, in order, once each; the beat targets add up to {video_length}; B14 runs 8–10 s; the tour stops add up to B14 and each place adds up to at most 1.5 s; every tour id exists in the design and `B14.rooms` matches the `INT` stops; the empty-room loop names its bare beat; no voiceover fields and no keys outside the Output; cards ≤ 6 words, ≥ 1.5 s, inside their beat, one on screen at a time; a QUESTION card only as Step 1.2 allows; STAGE, SPEC, NAME and QUESTION cards ≤ 1 per 10 s on average; spec cards end with “· CONCEPT”; no forbidden words, no source identity, no real-world claims; disclaimer and end card present; music length {video_length}; PROGRESS ≤ 1 per state and ≤ 15% of the running time; every beat named in story exists in `script.beats`; every room in `beats[].rooms` exists in `yacht_bible.rooms`; every beat respects the `operational_limits` of the features it shows.
- **WARN — editorial (reported, does not block):** a beat shorter than about 0.8 s; a hero B16 shorter than about 2 s or more than half covered by cards; fewer than two money shots outside the Step 1.9 list; an act without a money shot; a construction state (BS06–BS11) filling more than 2 consecutive beats; two beats in the same state that differ too little; an act with no new location or time of day.
- **JUDGE — story (≥ 8/10):** every beat showable without words; every beat plays its role; the joints read; obstacles plausible for shipbuilding (when used); central question answerable on screen (when there is one).
- **JUDGE — wordless clarity (≥ 8/10):**

| Criterion | Points |
| --- | --- |
| The opening works in the first seconds with sound off | 2 |
| The spine reads across the film without words | 2 |
| Each beat reads in the time it has | 2 |
| The tour shows varied, recognisable places | 2 |
| Hero is the most beautiful moment and the first full reveal | 2 |

### Quality gate

- [ ] Spine chosen from the design and carried by every beat
- [ ] All 17 roles present, in order; every adaptation true to the design
- [ ] Links written as concrete images
- [ ] Final cut exactly {video_length}; B14 8–10 s; each tour place ≤ 1.5 s
- [ ] Reveal ladder and room states respected; operational limits respected
- [ ] Motifs and first–last rhyme planned
- [ ] Emotion curve ready for music selection
- [ ] No narration anywhere
- [ ] Cards sparse, compliant and inside their beats
- [ ] Music brief and SFX plan complete
