### Gates

- **RULE (code):** LOA 110–180 m; specs in range or justified; every anchor within its word limit and the yacht and geometry anchors state the LOA figure; the finished surface names an exterior color; no forbidden words, no blocklisted names; ≤ 3 exterior colors with valid HEX; 3 innovations positioned; ≥ 10 rooms; name not near-matching the source or blocklist; every room and zone is one space of `canonical.spaces`, every id once, every reference to an existing id; a space\'s decks exist and its figures fit the yacht and those decks; connections join two different spaces, an adjacency has no users and a passage has users; every route runs over connections that join its consecutive spaces and admit its users; every innovation has its relations, and an effect only where it has one; every operational limit governs an existing innovation, part or space; a built-in referenced by a surface belongs to that room; the GEOMETRY ANCHOR contains no color.
- **JUDGE:** must-avoid satisfied; anchors are geometric, not adjectival; rooms are distinct from each other and organised for their use (≥ 8/10).
- **REVIEW (a person):** the design is read and approved on the Design screen; the model sheet is then rendered from it and approved by a person.
