- **RULE (code):** every `LOC` id once and used; ids exist (rooms and zones in the design, locations in this answer); `script_id` matches the script; every `evidence` quote is found verbatim in its field; every use, light, detail and shot change points to a beat or stop the background serves; a room background matches the `set_state` the script gives, at a tour stop too; an exterior background serves uses of one build-state kind and one surface; an `unplated` or `unresolved` entry names the space and state the script gives its use; every room state the script names, every beat and every tour stop is covered; every `match_bare_beat` has its continuity entry; a conflict names a background or a beat; no two backgrounds alike (same space, state, build-state kind and surface, condition and composition); no background id twice; a location detail never repeats a surface or fixture of its location; every `design_refs` id exists, the design gives its relation for the background\'s own space (`mounted_in` for `mounted`, `effect_in` and an effect for `effect`), the feature exists at the build state of every use where the design states it, and no location carries design features or the lighting signature; every `must_keep` rule of a designed space that applies at the uses of a background is accounted for in its `keeps`, once each, and only those; the lighting signature only on a finished room or an exterior area at a finished build state; a finished room has the design\'s materials, or its anchor where the design lists none; `fit` matches the beats that stand on each location (a beat at a build state holds the full yacht, a `scale_model` beat the scale model) and a place that holds the yacht, a module or a model is not smaller than it; an enclosed `kind` is `bounded` and never `open` overhead; no real names; `status` is `partial` while a conflict or an unresolved use is open; the prompt sent to render is the prompt shown and approved.
- **WARNING (code, a person decides):** two locations alike in every fixed field (kind, space, size, clear height, surfaces, equipment, palette), perhaps one place; a `bare` or `fitout` room whose text names a word of its finished materials; a first must-show item that names no feature of the space; chandelier, gold, marble or another upgrade the space\'s design does not give; a colour temperature the design does not state and no assumption lists; the lighting signature on a background whose uses are not at night, dusk, dawn or blue hour, or that shares no word with the space\'s design; a design feature whose build state the design does not state; a `must_keep` rule no plate of its space keeps in frame; a rule whose build state some uses of a background reach and others do not (it is left out); a background of a space that rises through several decks whose `scope` names none of them; an anchor holding words the room\'s fields do not; an exterior\'s `surroundings` that shares a word with the area\'s own design text; a tour room whose state the script does not give; a location text that names the yacht or a part of it; a composition that seems to describe a camera move; a background seen only briefly with many must-show details; an exterior background serving an `H1` beat; dimensions that are assumptions, unverified or short of the recommended working room.
