### Gates

- **RULE (code):** LOA 110–180 m; specs in range or justified; every anchor within its word limit and the yacht and geometry anchors state the LOA figure; the finished surface names an exterior color; no forbidden words, no blocklisted names; ≤ 3 exterior colors with valid HEX; 3 innovations positioned; ≥ 10 rooms; name not near-matching the source or blocklist; every room and zone is one space of `canonical.spaces`, every id once, every reference to an existing id; a space\'s decks exist and its figures fit the yacht and those decks; connections join two different spaces, an adjacency has no users and a passage has users, a door or opening joins two spaces that share a deck; every route runs over connections that join its consecutive spaces and admit its users; every innovation has its relations, and an effect only where it has one; each visible element or named group of an innovation once; an innovation relation has its six keys only; every measure of an innovation is named `n<id>_<name>` in lowercase for an existing innovation, gives its `quantity` with the unit of that quantity (`length` `m`, `volume` `m3`, `mass` `t`) and a positive value, and no two names of measures are the same once normalised; every key in `measures` is a `length` of that innovation; every operational limit governs an existing innovation, part or space; a built-in referenced by a surface belongs to that room; the GEOMETRY ANCHOR contains no color; the model sheet\'s own checks open the design — coordinate system, base data, no conflicting source fields, an MS8 target.
- **WARNING (code, a person decides):** a `must_not` whose description opens with "do not", "no" or "not"; an identity rule that speaks of spec cards, titles, headlines, captions, subtitles, on-screen text, narration or voice-over; an innovation whose text describes repeated parts (facets, pockets, louvres, panels, rows…) with no `visible_elements`.
- **JUDGE:** must-avoid satisfied; anchors are geometric, not adjectival; rooms are distinct from each other and organised for their use (≥ 8/10).
- **REVIEW (a person):** the design is read and approved on the Design screen; the model sheet is then rendered from it and approved by a person.
